---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "October 16, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — DepositRescue | Tenant Data Protection"
  description="Learn how DepositRescue protects your personal information, rental lease data, and certified mail delivery records with strict confidentiality and security."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-border pb-8">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-3 py-1 text-xs font-mono font-medium text-text-secondary">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-success"></span>
        Data Protection &amp; Confidentiality
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-primary sm:text-4xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-text-muted">
        Last Updated: {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Intro -->
    <section class="space-y-4 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        DepositRescue (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) operates getdepositrescue.com to provide self-help legal calculations and certified demand letter automation for residential tenants.
      </p>
      <p>
        We believe that personal and financial information entered while defending your tenant rights deserves maximum confidentiality. We do not sell your personal data to landlords, credit agencies, or advertising brokers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 1. Information Collected -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">A. Information You Provide Voluntarily:</strong> When using the Deposit Recovery Calculator or generating demand letters, you may provide your state of tenancy, move-out dates, deposit sums, deductions in dispute, names, and mailing addresses for USPS delivery.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">B. Payment Data:</strong> If you order USPS Certified Mail fulfillment ($29.99), transactions are processed directly by our PCI-DSS Level 1 certified payment partners (e.g., Stripe). DepositRescue never stores raw credit card numbers or security CVVs on our servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-text-primary">C. Technical Usage Data:</strong> Standard server access logs including IP address, browser type, and timestamps to ensure infrastructure stability, prevent fraud, and detect abusive traffic.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. How Data is Used -->
    <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <li>Evaluating state landlord-tenant deadlines and computing statutory multiplier penalties.</li>
        <li>Compiling personalized legal demand notices and printable PDF exhibits.</li>
        <li>Dispatching physical letters via USPS Certified Mail with Electronic Return Receipt through licensed postal fulfillment infrastructure (Lob / PostGrid).</li>
        <li>Communicating delivery confirmation and USPS barcode tracking updates.</li>
        <li>Complying with applicable tax, legal, and regulatory requirements.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Third-Party Sharing -->
    <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">3. Information Sharing &amp; Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        We share your information strictly with vetted service providers necessary to operate our service:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 pt-1 text-xs">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-3">
          <strong class="text-text-primary">USPS &amp; Print Fulfillment:</strong>
          <p class="mt-1 text-text-muted">Mailing names and addresses are transmitted securely to postal print centers solely to print and deliver your certified demand envelope.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-3">
          <strong class="text-text-primary">Payment Gateways:</strong>
          <p class="mt-1 text-text-muted">Payment tokens are processed via encrypted HTTPS directly with PCI-certified providers (Stripe).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Security & Data Retention -->
    <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">4. Data Security &amp; Retention</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        All data transfers are protected by TLS 1.3 encryption. Calculation inputs processed in your browser remain client-side until you explicitly order certified mail dispatch. Physical letter records and tracking metadata are retained for up to 180 days to allow verification during small claims court proceedings, after which records can be purged upon request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. User Rights (CCPA / GDPR) -->
    <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">5. Your Privacy Rights (CCPA &amp; GDPR)</h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Under state statutes such as the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and international frameworks, you have the right to request access to the personal data we hold about you, request corrections, or demand immediate deletion. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@getdepositrescue.com" class="text-text-primary underline hover:text-emerald-400">privacy@getdepositrescue.com</a> or via our <a href="/contact" class="text-text-primary underline hover:text-emerald-400">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
